[5267]="70050B41\n1\tComplete scaling instances in the Grey Mountains.\t\n2\tComplete the Glimmerdeep Instance\030Complete the Thikil-gundu Instance\030Complete the Caverns of Thrumfall Instance\tComplete each of the Grey Mountain instances, on any difficulty level, weekly. The scaling instance cluster can be found in the Instance Join panel.\n",
[5268]="7002D5B7\n1\tStay with the horse and use the right emote\tThe horse can be found out in the Horse-fields.\n2\tTell Éogar what happened\t\n",
[5269]="70067E7F\n1\tDefeat freebooters (0/8)\tAnyâmat thinks it would be a great idea to pick fights with random freebooters so that she might experience the rough and tumble life of a sailor. Willing freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.\n2\tTalk to Anyâmat\tThe first freebooter you spoke to wasn't interested in fighting. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next. Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzir.\n3\tChallenge freebooters (0/8)\tThe first freebooter you spoke to isn't interested in fighting. Try challenging one of her friends. Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.\n4\tTalk to Anyâmat\tThe second freebooter you spoke to isn't interested in fighting. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next. Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.\n5\tMake friends (2/4)\tThe second freebooter you spoke to wasn't interested in fighting. Anyâmat has decided to change strategies and wants to make friends with these freebooters instead. Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.\n6\tMake friends (3/4) Talk to Anyâmat\tThe third freebooter gave you and Anyâmat some grilled fish. Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next. Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.\n7\tMake friends (3/4)\tAnyâmat wants to make friends with all four freebooters on this little island. Freebooters may be found on a tiny island north-west of Halrax.\n8\tMake friends (4/4) Talk to Anyâmat\tAnyâmat has made unexpected friends with the freebooters she was intending to instigate! Talk to Anyâmat about what to do next. Anyâmat may be summoned by using Anyâmat's whistle from your inventory. Anyâmat may only be summoned while in and around Zamarzîr.\n",
[5270]="70022D7A\n1\tTalk to Corunir at Aughaire\tAughaire is an encampment of Hillmen, north through the Ram Dúath. Corunir's letter requests aid for the warriors standing against the oppressive Angmarim.\n",
[5271]="7000B102\n1\tTalk to Gelbes at Glân Vraig and complete a patrol through the Ettenmoors as a Ranger (Cost: 500 Commendations)\tGelbes is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. Speak with her to call a ranger to the Ettenmoors. The Rangers will assist in retaking Tol Ascarnen, but they request that you take the place of a Ranger in Eriador while they come to the Ettenmoors to fight in your stead.\n2\tTalk to Gelbes\tGelbes is at Glân Vraig in the Ettenmoors. A Ranger came to the Ettenmoors in your stead and fought valiantly while you patrolled Eriador in their stead.\n",
[5272]="700164DA\n1\tPoison the food\tThe lizard-food can be found at The Drowned Deep, west of Hulwul-nefekh. Gyrgir says that a powerful lizard, Stonecrest, often feeds on grodbog-corpses. He has crafted a powerful poison to sprinkle on the food. Once Stonecrest eats it, Gyrgir believes you may have a chance to defeat it.\n2\tTalk to Gyrgir in Hulwul-nefekh\tGyrgir is in Hulwul-nefekh, east of The Drowned Deep. Gyrgir will be pleased to know his poison worked and that Stonecrest will devour no more dwarves.\n",
[5273]="7000A8BA\n1\tDefeat Angmarim in Annúminas (total: 20)\tAngmarim can be found everywhere among the streets of Annúminas, on the south-west shore of Lake Nenuial. Ringlor hopes that by lending your arm to the struggle, you might help turn the tide of the battle for Annúminas.\n2\tTalk to Ringlor\tRinglor is at the Ranger-camp on the island of Tinnudir, in Evendim. The Ranger Ringlor asked you to join the battle against the Angmarim in the city of Annúminas, and you took part in the struggle. Now you should return with news of your victories.\n",
[5274]="70001119\n1\tDefeat spiders in the Wovenvales (total: 10)\tSpiders have made their home in the Wovenvales of the North Trollshaws, north of Thoroniel's camp. Thoroniel has asked you to defeat spiders in the Wovenvales, advising you to bring allies.\n2\tTalk to Thoroniel\tThoroniel is in the North Trollshaws, just south of the Wovenvales in the north-west corner. Thoroniel is waiting to hear that you have defeated the spiders which stalk the Wovenvales.\n",
[5275]="70015210\n1\tHelp Ansurr\030Help Gyrgir\030Help Thrand\tAnsurr and the other dwarves are at Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works. Ansurr has asked you to assist the other dwarves with their ideas about how to defend against the vile growth.\n2\tTalk to Ansurr at Hulwul-nefekh\tAnsurr is in Hulwul-nefekh in central Water-works. You should return to Ansurr and inform him you have aided his companions with their ideas.\n",
[5276]="70017510\n1\tReturn the ring to Eilíefr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect General Talug's ring (quantity: see journal)\tGeneral Talug can be found in Fil Gashan, far to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Eilíefr has asked you to defeat General Talug to demonstrate your excellence, and return with his ring when you are done.\n",
[5277]="7001751E\n1\tKill enemies in Fil Gashan (total: 80)\tFil Gashan is south-west of the Twenty-first Hall. The dwarf Geirr has challenged you to make your way into Fil Gashan and defeat many Orcs therein.\n2\tReturn to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall\tThe dwarf Geirr is in the Twenty-first hall, north-east of Fil Gashan Geirr will wish to hear if you have been brave enough to enter Fil Gashan and face the Orcs in battle.\n",
[5278]="70017519\n1\tFil Gashan is far to the south-west of the Twenty-first Hall, and General Talug can be found in the depths of that place. Sigurd has challenged you to use stealth and wit to conquer General Talug, the leader of a great Orc-host, without defeating too many of his sentries.\t\n2\tReturn to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall\tSigurd awaits news of your foray in the Twenty-first Hall, north-east of Fil Gashan. General Talug has fallen by your hand and you have successfully moved through the uruk sentries without being much detected. Sigurd will wish to hear if you have met all the terms of his difficult challenge.\n",
[5279]="70057D6F\n1\tFind and retrieve abandoned mugs in the Prancing Pony (total: 8)\030Coax drunken revellers off tables in the Prancing Pony (total: 6)\tDrunken revellers and forsaken mugs can be found throughout the Prancing Pony in Bree. Barliman has asked you to coax drunken revellers off the tables before they can kick more of his crockery into the corners of the Prancing Pony. He has also asked you to gather any mugs abandoned by drunken revellers in unusual spots in the inn.\n2\tDeliver the mugs to Barliman Butterbur\tDeliver the mugs to Barliman Butterbur at the entrance to the inn.\n",
[5280]="70042EDD\n1\tDagor and Indir can be found at the keep in Arnach. Baranor has asked you to help his two captains, Dagor and Indir, protect the town from the Haradrim.\t\n2\tTalk to Baranor\tBaranor can be found at the keep in Arnach. You have helped Dagor and Indir work against the invading Haradrim, as Baranor asked. Now you should return to Baranor in Arnach.\n",
})
